      tldr: 'Pool cleaning in Albuquerque runs around $29 a visit, with a range of $27–$31 a visit based on pool size and type (HomeBlue\u2019s Albuquerque page). Weekly service — four visits a month — comes to $107–$125 a month on that same page. Budget $1,600–$1,900 a year all in for cleaning, maintenance, and opening and closing the pool.',
      faq: [
        { q: 'How much does pool cleaning cost in Albuquerque?', a: 'Around $29 a visit, ranging from $27 to $31 depending on pool size and type (HomeBlue\u2019s Albuquerque page). Weekly service at four visits a month runs $107–$125, and annual maintenance including opening and closing runs $1,600–$1,900.' },
        { q: 'Are chemicals included in the price?', a: 'Ask before you book. A standard Albuquerque cleaning package typically includes measuring chemistry levels and adding chemicals, along with vacuuming, cleaning accessories, checking or backwashing the filter, and checking fixtures (HomeBlue). Some quotes bill chemicals on top of the visit price, which is why two quotes for the same pool can look far apart.' },
        { q: 'Does my pool need weekly service in Albuquerque?', a: 'In summer, yes for most pools. Strong sun at this elevation burns off chlorine fast, and spring and summer wind keeps adding dust. Every-other-week can work in the cooler months for a covered or lightly used pool, but a 14-day gap in July is how a clear pool turns cloudy.' },
        { q: 'My pool is already green. What will that cost?', a: 'No Albuquerque-specific green-pool price is published. Nationally, a one-time cleaning runs $148–$413 on Thumbtack, with most people paying around $201, and HomeGuide puts a first-time cleaning at $150–$350 — national figures, not Albuquerque quotes. A badly neglected pool can take several visits before weekly service can start.' },
        { q: 'How do I find a pool cleaner near me in Albuquerque?', a: 'Search Van Squads by ZIP — 87114 on the northwest side, covering Ventana Ranch and Paradise Hills, is where all four listed pool businesses work — then request a quote from the profile.' }
      ],
      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Albuquerque pool owners actually pay</h3><p>Albuquerque-specific figures from HomeBlue, plus national figures labeled as national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Pool service</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Per visit, Albuquerque (HomeBlue)</td><td>$27–$31, around $29</td></tr><tr><td>Two visits a month, Albuquerque</td><td>$53–$62</td></tr><tr><td>Three visits a month, Albuquerque</td><td>$80–$94</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly — four visits a month, Albuquerque</td><td>$107–$125 per month</td></tr><tr><td>Annual maintenance, Albuquerque (cleaning, maintenance, opening and closing)</td><td>$1,600–$1,900 per year</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly or biweekly service, national (HomeGuide)</td><td>$80–$150 per month</td></tr><tr><td>One-time cleaning, national (Thumbtack)</td><td>$148–$413, most pay around $201</td></tr><tr><td>First-time cleaning, national (HomeGuide)</td><td>$150–$350</td></tr><tr><td>Pool opening or closing, national (HomeGuide)</td><td>$300–$550</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Read the Albuquerque number for what it is. A $29 visit is a cleaning visit — skimming, vacuuming, brushing, baskets, a chemistry check. Not a repair call, and not a rescue for a pool that has gone green. This is where people overpay: one quote is a flat month with chemicals in it, another is per visit with chemicals on top. Ask what is included before you compare the two.</p><p>The national check lines up — Albuquerque\u2019s weekly $107–$125 sits inside HomeGuide\u2019s national $80–$150 a month.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Albuquerque?</h3><p><strong>Wind and dust.</strong> Spring winds lift fine dust off the West Mesa and the dry arroyos and drop it straight into your pool. It settles on the floor, fills the skimmer basket, and makes the filter work harder. A windy week in April can do more to a northwest-side pool in Ventana Ranch or Paradise Hills than a calm month in winter.</p><p><strong>Sun, evaporation, and hard water.</strong> Albuquerque sits a mile up. The sun is strong, chlorine burns off fast in summer, and dry air pulls water out — so you top it off more often. The fill water here is hard, and every top-off adds calcium. That is the white scale on your tile. Keeping chemistry balanced in that cycle is the real job.</p><p><strong>Your pool\u2019s setup.</strong> HomeBlue lists a large pool, difficult access, trees dropping debris, and a sandy location as reasons a quote lands higher, and a small or salt water pool as reasons it lands lower. A salt system changes the chemical bill, not the need for brushing and vacuuming.</p><h3>How to pay less without a green pool</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Stay weekly in summer.</strong> Cutting visits in July is how a $29 visit turns into a one-time rescue. Nationally a first-time or one-time cleaning runs $150–$413 — roughly five to ten regular visits.</li><li><strong>Empty the baskets between visits.</strong> After a windy day, a packed skimmer basket blocks circulation and strains the pump. Two minutes with the basket saves the filter and the pump.</li><li><strong>Cover the pool when a dust day is coming.</strong> A cover keeps grit out, slows evaporation, and holds chlorine longer.</li><li><strong>Plan opening and closing, don\u2019t drift into them.</strong> HomeBlue\u2019s $1,600–$1,900 annual figure already includes opening and closing. Nationally those run $300–$550 each, so a pool left to sit all winter usually costs more to bring back.</li></ul><h3>An Albuquerque pool service listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Atlantis Pool Service LLC</strong> is a pool cleaning and maintenance business listed on Van Squads, offering pool cleaning and maintenance at your location in Albuquerque ZIP 87114, on the northwest side — the Ventana Ranch and Paradise Hills area. See its listing and request a quote: <a href="/business/atlantis-pool-service-llc">Atlantis Pool Service LLC on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 4 pool cleaning and maintenance businesses in the Albuquerque metro, and all four cover ZIP 87114. Pool coverage on the directory is concentrated on the northwest side for now, unlike house cleaning, which covers most of the metro. Enter your ZIP to see who covers your neighborhood: <a href="/#/browse?zip=87114">search pool cleaning near 87114</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/pool-cleaning-maintenance/albuquerque/\">Pool cleaning & maintenance in Albuquerque</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Need the house cleaned too? See the Albuquerque house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-albuquerque/">how much does house cleaning cost in Albuquerque?</a></p>{{img:2}}'
