      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Dallas–Fort Worth pool owners actually pay</h3><p>Dallas figures from HomeBlue and Dallas operators that publish prices, plus national figures labeled as national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Pool service</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Per visit, Dallas (HomeBlue)</td><td>$27–$32, around $30</td></tr><tr><td>Four visits a month, Dallas (HomeBlue)</td><td>$109–$128 per month</td></tr><tr><td>Annual maintenance, Dallas (HomeBlue)</td><td>$1,600–$1,900 per year</td></tr><tr><td>Partial weekly plan, Dallas (Blue Science)</td><td>From $149 per month</td></tr><tr><td>Full weekly plan, Dallas (Blue Science)</td><td>From $209 per month</td></tr><tr><td>Flat weekly plan, Dallas (Golden Hour Pools)</td><td>$250 per month</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly or biweekly service, national (HomeGuide)</td><td>$80–$150 per month</td></tr><tr><td>One-time cleaning, national (Thumbtack)</td><td>$148–$413, most pay around $201</td></tr><tr><td>Pool opening or closing, national (HomeGuide)</td><td>$300–$550</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Why the gap between $109 and $250? They are not the same job. The HomeBlue figure is a cleaning visit. A plan adds chemicals, equipment checks and a report, and full service adds netting and vacuuming. Blue Science charges $60 more for full than partial in Dallas — that $60 is netting and vacuuming. Golden Hour\u2019s $250 includes filter cleaning. Blue Science charges it on top, at $179 every 3–4 months.</p><p>This is where people overpay. Compare what is in the quote, not just the number.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Dallas–Fort Worth?</h3><p><strong>Heat and hard water.</strong> Dallas tap water is hard and leaves calcium scale at the tile line, and July heat burns through chlorine in days (Blue Science\u2019s Dallas page). You top the pool off, you add more hard water, scale builds again. Keeping the water balanced is most of the weekly job.</p><p><strong>Trees and pollen.</strong> Pecans, live oaks and cedar elms over older Dallas neighborhoods — Lakewood, Kessler Park, Casa Linda and Forest Hills, the ones Blue Science names on its Dallas route — drop leaves all year and pollen in spring. Leaves that sit stain plaster and feed algae. A pool under those trees needs more work than one in full sun in a newer Plano subdivision.</p><p><strong>Winter does not pause it.</strong> Leaves keep falling in January, and a freeze week can crack an unprotected pump. Blue Science says its winter visit gets shorter, but the water test, baskets and equipment check still happen weekly.</p><p><strong>Your pool\u2019s setup.</strong> HomeBlue lists a large pool, difficult access, trees and more accessories as reasons a quote lands higher, and a small or salt water pool as reasons it lands lower.</p><h3>How to pay less without a green pool</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Stay weekly in summer.</strong> Skipping July visits is how a regular plan turns into a cleanup bill. In Dallas, Golden Hour charges $350 for a one-time green-pool clean — more than a month of weekly service.</li><li><strong>Take the partial plan only if you will do the work.</strong> At $149 a month, you handle netting and vacuuming and the pro handles chemistry, brushing, baskets and equipment checks. If you will not net the pool, the $209 full plan is cheaper than a rescue.</li><li><strong>Empty the baskets between visits.</strong> After a storm, a packed basket strains the pump. Two minutes.</li><li><strong>Ask about filter cleaning before you sign.</strong> Included, like Golden Hour\u2019s plan, or billed every few months, like Blue Science\u2019s $179? That line changes the real cost.</li></ul><h3>A Dallas–Fort Worth pool service listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Gohlke Pools</strong> is a pool cleaning and maintenance business listed on Van Squads, offering pool cleaning and maintenance at your location in Denton ZIP 76210. See its listing and request a quote: <a href="/business/gohlke-pools">Gohlke Pools on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 10 pool cleaning businesses in the Dallas–Fort Worth metro, in two clusters for now — five cover Plano ZIP 75023, and five cover Denton ZIP 76210. Enter your ZIP to see who covers your area: <a href="/#/browse?zip=76210">search pool cleaning near 76210</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/pool-cleaning-maintenance/dallas-fort-worth/\">Pool cleaning & maintenance in Dallas–Fort Worth</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>In Plano? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=75023">search pool cleaning near 75023</a>.</p>{{img:2}}'
