      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Dallas–Fort Worth homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Local figures from Angi, Thumbtack and Care.com city pages and a Dallas operator, plus national figures labeled as national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Average visit, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>$163</td></tr><tr><td>Hiring a pro, Dallas (Thumbtack)</td><td>$181–$322 (low $118, high $484)</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>About $50, range $25–$75</td></tr><tr><td>Listed cleaner, Dallas (Care.com)</td><td>$21.61/hr average</td></tr><tr><td>Listed cleaner, Fort Worth (Care.com)</td><td>$19.89/hr average</td></tr><tr><td>Top pros, Fort Worth (Thumbtack)</td><td>$55–$140</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, Dallas company (Dallas Maids)</td><td>$140–$280</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, Dallas company (Dallas Maids)</td><td>$220–$440</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out clean, Dallas company (Dallas Maids)</td><td>$350–$600+</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, 2,200 sq ft, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>$220–$440</td></tr><tr><td>Deep / move-out, 2,200 sq ft, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>$550 / $770</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly / biweekly visit, Dallas (Angi)</td><td>$70–$190 / $95–$240</td></tr><tr><td>Per visit, national (HomeGuide)</td><td>$120–$280</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Those hourly numbers are not measuring the same hire. Care.com’s $21.61 is a listed individual cleaner. Angi’s $50 is the company rate, and a company often sends two people — about $100 an hour for the whole visit.</p><p>This is where people overpay. Compare the finished price for your home, not the hourly number.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Dallas–Fort Worth?</h3><p><strong>Size, first.</strong> Angi prices Dallas by the square foot: a standard clean runs $0.10–$0.20 per square foot, so a 1,500 square foot home runs $150–$300 and the median 2,200 square foot home runs $220–$440. Each extra bathroom adds $10–$40.</p><p><strong>Dust and tile.</strong> Angi calls out Dallas dust and allergens, and notes tile floors are common in Dallas kitchens, bathrooms and laundry rooms because they suit the hot climate — grout takes time. Older homes in Lakewood (75214), White Rock (75218) and Lake Highlands (75243) carry more of that work than a new build in Plano.</p><p><strong>Humidity on the Fort Worth side.</strong> Thumbtack’s Fort Worth guidance flags the humid climate: mold in bathrooms and warped wood floors in older homes need slower work, and that can move a Fort Worth quote up even when the hourly listings look lower.</p><p><strong>How often they come.</strong> Angi puts a biweekly Dallas cleaning at $95–$240 against $120–$290 for a monthly one.</p><h3>Standard, deep, or move-out — which one are you actually buying?</h3><p>A standard clean covers the regular rooms: kitchen surfaces, bathrooms, floors, dusting. A deep clean adds the buildup — about $0.25 per square foot on Angi’s Dallas page, $220–$440 on Dallas Maids’ list.</p><p>Move-out is the priciest: about $0.35 per square foot (Angi), $770 at 2,200 square feet, $350–$600 or more (Dallas Maids). If the home is not empty, you are paying for work you do not need.</p><p>Add-ons are priced apart. On Angi’s Dallas list: fridge $10–$40, oven $20–$40, windows $4–$10 per window, laundry $5–$20 a load.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get a clean house</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Go recurring.</strong> Weekly or biweekly visits cost less per visit because the home never gets far behind.</li><li><strong>Book the deep clean once, then maintain.</strong> Pay the deep price first, then drop to the standard rate.</li><li><strong>Compare finished prices, not hourly rates.</strong> One cleaner for four hours and a two-person company done in two can cost about the same.</li><li><strong>Name the add-ons in writing.</strong> Fridge, oven, inside windows. If it is not named, it is not included.</li></ul><h3>A Dallas–Fort Worth house cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Organically Maid</strong> is a house cleaning business listed on Van Squads, offering house cleaning at your location across Fort Worth-area ZIPs including 76102, 76107, 76179, 76126 and 76137 — 28 service ZIPs in all. See its listing and request a quote: <a href="/business/organically-maid">Organically Maid on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 20 house cleaning businesses in the metro, in three clusters — eight cover Lakewood, Dallas ZIP 75214, seven cover Plano ZIP 75093, and five cover Saginaw ZIP 76179: <a href="/#/browse?zip=76102">search house cleaning near 76102</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/house-cleaning/dallas-fort-worth/\">House cleaning in Dallas–Fort Worth</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>In Dallas? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=75214">search house cleaning near 75214</a>. In Plano? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=75093">search house cleaning near 75093</a>.</p>{{img:2}}'
