      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Dallas–Fort Worth pet owners actually pay</h3><p>DFW prices by dog size, from a DFW operator’s published 2026 table:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Service in Dallas–Fort Worth</th><th>Bath &amp; brush</th><th>Full groom</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Small dog, under 20 lbs</td><td>$65–$88</td><td>$78–$105</td></tr><tr><td>Medium dog, 20–50 lbs</td><td>$88–$118</td><td>$105–$145</td></tr><tr><td>Large dog, 50–80 lbs</td><td>$112–$148</td><td>$132–$178</td></tr><tr><td>XL dog, 80+ lbs</td><td>$142–$182</td><td>$165–$222</td></tr><tr><td>Doodle breeds</td><td>$98–$145</td><td>$118–$188</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A second Dallas–Fort Worth operator, America’s Paw Spaw, lands higher: bath packages run $100–$150 for short coats and $110–$185 for longer coats by weight, and a groom package with a haircut runs $130 up to 20 lbs to $250 over 90 lbs. Two honest DFW quotes for the same dog can sit $40 apart. Ask what is included first.</p><p>Groomit’s Dallas page puts a full groom starting around $89 — the small-dog end of the table above. Care.com is a different hire: pet grooming in Dallas averages $12.60 an hour there as of October 2026, for an individual groomer by the hour, not a van visit. Nationally, Thumbtack puts dog grooming at $60–$80 on average, with bath, haircut, nails, ears, and glands bundled at $110–$160 by dog size. National figures, not DFW quotes.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Dallas–Fort Worth?</h3><p><strong>Size and coat, first.</strong> The table is really a time table. A large double-coated dog takes longer to wash, dry, and brush out than a short-coated small dog, and a doodle costs more than a same-size short coat because its coat keeps growing and mats.</p><p><strong>Texas heat.</strong> Summer heat runs May through September here, with early morning scheduling prioritized (DFW Mobile Dog Grooming). In a Garland or Arlington August, the good slots go first. Book the morning.</p><p><strong>How far out you are.</strong> Pricing is consistent across most of the metroplex, and a travel surcharge may apply to far outer suburbs. Van Squads’ coverage shows why: listed groomers cluster in Arlington (76018), Garland (75044), and Lewisville (75067). Inside a cluster you are a route stop. Well past it, you are a special trip.</p><p><strong>Mats and add-ons are paid time.</strong> On America’s Paw Spaw’s list, de-shedding starts at $25 and matting starts at $40, with nail filing at $15 and oral care at $10. A matted doodle in Mesquite is not the $118 starting price anymore.</p><p>Most breeds do fine every 6–8 weeks. Poodles, doodles, and other coats that keep growing need it every 4–6 weeks. Kept on that schedule, a dog is a routine visit at the table price. Left three months and matted, the same dog pays more and takes longer.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse groom</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Take the bath and brush between haircuts.</strong> At $65–$118 for small and medium dogs, it keeps the full groom routine.</li><li><strong>Stay on a 4–6 week schedule for doodles and long coats.</strong> Shorter visits cost less than rescue grooms.</li><li><strong>Brush between visits.</strong> Mats start at $40 on a local list — a few minutes at home avoids that fee.</li><li><strong>Compare what is included.</strong> One quote bundles nails, ears, and glands; another adds them at $10–$25 each.</li></ul><h3>A Dallas–Fort Worth mobile groomer listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Zoomin Groomin Mesquite &amp; South Garland</strong> is a mobile pet grooming business listed on Van Squads, offering mobile pet grooming at your location across five east Dallas–Fort Worth ZIPs — 75044 and 75043 in Garland, 75088 in Rowlett, and 75150 and 75182 in Mesquite and Sunnyvale. See its listing and request a quote: <a href="/business/zoomin-groomin-mesquite-south-garland">Zoomin Groomin Mesquite &amp; South Garland on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 10 mobile pet grooming businesses in the Dallas–Fort Worth metro, in three clusters — four cover Arlington ZIP 76018, three cover Garland ZIP 75044, and three cover Lewisville ZIP 75067. Enter your ZIP to see who covers your neighborhood: <a href="/#/browse?zip=75044">search mobile pet grooming near 75044</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/mobile-pet-grooming/dallas-fort-worth/\">Mobile pet grooming in Dallas–Fort Worth</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>In Arlington? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=76018">search mobile pet grooming near 76018</a>. In Lewisville? Try: <a href="/#/browse?zip=75067">search mobile pet grooming near 75067</a>.</p><p>Need the house cleaned too? See the Dallas–Fort Worth house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-dallas-fort-worth/">How much does house cleaning cost in Dallas–Fort Worth?</a></p>{{img:2}}'
