      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Boise homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Boise and Meridian pages, plus one national row labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pressure washing / house / concrete / deck &amp; fence, starting price, Boise (Window Genie of Boise)</td><td>$199</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, 1,500–2,000 sq ft, Boise (HomeBlue)</td><td>$400–$700, average about $500</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, 2,000–3,000 sq ft, Boise (HomeBlue)</td><td>$600–$1,000</td></tr><tr><td>House wash, 4,000–5,000 sq ft, Boise (HomeBlue)</td><td>$1,000–$1,700</td></tr><tr><td>Driveway, 40 x 20 ft, Boise (HomeBlue)</td><td>$150–$270, average about $210</td></tr><tr><td>Driveway, 100 x 20 ft, Boise (HomeBlue)</td><td>$380–$670</td></tr><tr><td>Deck or patio, 200 sq ft, Boise (HomeBlue)</td><td>$70–$110, average about $90</td></tr><tr><td>Per sq ft of property size (Thumbtack, Boise page)</td><td>$0.10–$0.17</td></tr><tr><td>Power washing, per hour, Meridian (HomeYou)</td><td>$50–$160/hr</td></tr><tr><td>House / siding wash (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$170–$360</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $199 quote and a $500 quote can both be honest — one is a starting price for a smaller job, the other is a full 1,500 to 2,000 sq ft house. Ask what size and which surfaces the quote covers before you compare the totals.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Boise?</h3><p><strong>Dust, pollen, and wildfire ash.</strong> Fine dust and pollen from sagebrush and farmland sit on siding and concrete most of the year, and late-summer smoke leaves ash on shaded north walls (That 1 Painter, Treasure Valley). A light film is a quick wash. A wall that went through fire season untouched takes solution and dwell time.</p><p><strong>Old wood in the North End, newer builds in Meridian.</strong> Older North End (83703) homes have chalkier paint and original wood siding that will not take maximum pressure. Newer builds in Meridian, Eagle, and Star can take a stronger wash (That 1 Painter). Same size, different method, different price.</p><p><strong>Size, height, and access.</strong> HomeBlue prices a Boise house by size — $400–$700 at 1,500 to 2,000 sq ft, up to $1,000–$1,700 at 4,000 to 5,000 sq ft. Two stories, tight access, and landscaping in the way push a quote up.</p><p><strong>Hot water costs more.</strong> Power washing uses heated water, and HomeBlue puts that at 10–15% more in Boise. You want it for grease and oil on a driveway in West Boise (83704). You do not need to pay for it on plain dust.</p><h3>Should your house be pressure washed or soft washed?</h3><p>Concrete driveways and walkways get high pressure. Painted siding and stucco get a soft wash — lower pressure with cleaning solution (That 1 Painter, Treasure Valley).</p><p>That split matters in Boise. Blast chalky North End paint and you strip it. Soft wash a Meridian driveway and the dust film comes off, but oil spots usually stay. A good quote names the method for each surface, in writing.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get it clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Bundle the flat work in one visit.</strong> Driveway, walkway, and patio in one stop in Meridian (83646) beats separate trips, each with its own starting price.</li><li><strong>Wash after fire season, not before it.</strong> Thumbtack\'s Boise page says a warm, sunny day is best, after the rainy season has passed. Waiting until the smoke clears means the wash is not coated in ash again a week later.</li><li><strong>Skip the hot-water upcharge unless you need it.</strong> Plain dust and ash do not need heated water. Oil and grease do — that is the 10–15% worth paying.</li><li><strong>Ask about a multi-service discount.</strong> Window Genie of Boise advertises 10% off multi-service work on its Boise price page. Other companies will not offer it unless you ask.</li></ul><h3>A Boise pressure washing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Idaho Hydro Wash</strong> is a pressure washing business listed on Van Squads, offering pressure washing at your location in ZIP 83646 in Meridian. See its listing: <a href="/business/idaho-hydro-wash">Idaho Hydro Wash on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 7 pressure washing businesses in the Boise metro, all covering Meridian ZIP 83646: <a href="/#/browse?zip=83646">search pressure washing near 83646</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href=\"/pressure-washing/boise/\">Pressure washing in Boise</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Got the outside clean and the inside is next? See the Boise house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-boise/">How much does house cleaning cost in Boise?</a></p>{{img:2}}'
