        { q: 'How much does a handyman cost in Boise?', a: '$40–$80 an hour, plus materials. Four hours runs $170–$330 and a full eight-hour day runs $350–$650 (HomeBlue, Boise).' }, { q: 'What is the minimum charge for a handyman?', a: 'Nationally, $75–$200 is a common minimum, with a $30–$80 trip charge on top for some pros (HomeGuide, national). That minimum is why one tiny job costs more than the hourly rate suggests — and why a bundled list is cheaper.' }, { q: 'Does a handyman need a license in Idaho?', a: 'Not for small work. Jobs under $2,000 in labor and materials do not require state registration in Idaho. Jobs at $2,000 or more require registration with the Idaho Contractors Board, and electrical, plumbing, and HVAC work always need a licensed trade.' }, { q: 'How much does a sprinkler blowout cost in Boise?', a: '$65–$85 for a typical 1–5 zone system. The Maintenance Shop in Meridian charges $65 early in the season, $75 for new requests Nov 10–30, and $85 from Dec 1. Beeline in Boise charges $80 flat for the first five zones, plus $7 per extra zone.' }, { q: 'How do I find a handyman near me in Boise?', a: 'Search Van Squads by ZIP. Coverage for handyman work sits in Meridian ZIPs 83642 and 83646, with 6 listed businesses covering the Boise metro.' }
