      tldr: 'In Omaha, a handyman runs $40–$80 an hour, plus materials (HomeBlue, Omaha). A half day — four hours — runs $160–$310, and a full day runs $320–$610. Most small jobs hit a minimum first: Thumbtack puts minimum rates at $60–$100, so one tiny fix rarely bills at one hour.',
