      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Omaha homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Omaha and Nebraska pages, plus a national figure labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Deep clean, average home, Omaha (Hautch Cleaning)</td><td>$240–$450+</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, 2,000 sq ft home, Omaha (Hautch Cleaning)</td><td>$300–$480</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, custom scope, per labor hour, Omaha (Hautch Cleaning)</td><td>$45–$65</td></tr><tr><td>Deep cleaning, Omaha (HomeGuide, Omaha page)</td><td>$230–$600</td></tr><tr><td>Standard house cleaning, Omaha (HomeGuide, Omaha page)</td><td>$90–$180</td></tr><tr><td>Deep cleaning, Nebraska (MaidProfit, Nebraska-wide)</td><td>$215–$425, average $310</td></tr><tr><td>Cleaner by the hour, Omaha (MaidProfit, Omaha row)</td><td>$24–$40 per cleaner</td></tr><tr><td>Cleaner by the hour, Omaha (Care.com, Nov 2026)</td><td>$20.58/hr starting</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, national average (Angi, national)</td><td>$260 — most pay $180–$375</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $240 quote and a $480 quote can both be honest. The first is a home cleaned regularly that needs the detail work caught up. The second is a first visit after months of buildup, priced off 6–10 labor hours for a 2,000 sq ft home. Compare checklists and labor hours, not just totals.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Omaha?</h3><p><strong>How long since the last real clean.</strong> Hautch expects 5–12 labor hours depending on size and buildup. A home in ZIP 68106 deep cleaned last fall is a short job. One that has gone a year is priced like a reset, because it is one.</p><p><strong>Winter is coming, and last winter is still in the house.</strong> Spring and fall are the ideal times in Omaha, post-winter salt and dust and before holiday hosting (Hautch). MaidProfit says the same from the Nebraska side: harsh winters create strong demand for spring deep cleaning. A fall clean clears the vents, baseboards and blinds before the house closes up again.</p><p><strong>The basement counts.</strong> Nebraska homes often have basements that add a lot of cleaning area (MaidProfit). A finished basement in Omaha is not a free extra room. Say up front whether it is in or out.</p><p><strong>Add-ons are priced on top.</strong> Inside the oven and fridge are on request on Hautch\'s Omaha list, and windows and grout work add to the labor hours. Nationally, Angi puts cleaning inside a kitchen appliance at $10–$50 per appliance — small money, but only if you named it before the visit.</p><h3>Deep clean or standard clean — what does the extra money buy?</h3><p>A standard clean in Omaha runs $90–$180 on HomeGuide\'s Omaha page. It maintains the surfaces: kitchen, bathrooms, floors, dusting what is easy to reach.</p><p>A deep clean adds the buildup work on Hautch\'s Omaha list: baseboards, vents, high dusting, blinds, a detailed kitchen and bathroom scrub, grout attention, and inside the oven or fridge on request. If nobody has wiped a vent cover or a baseboard in a year, a standard clean will not catch you up.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get a real deep clean</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Book the deep clean once, then keep it up.</strong> Standard cleaning statewide runs $100–$225, and recurring clients pay less per visit (MaidProfit). Pay the reset price once, in November, and let cheaper visits hold it.</li><li><strong>Declutter before they arrive.</strong> Hautch\'s prep rule for Omaha: don\'t pre-clean, just declutter surfaces and clear access to sinks, appliances and outlets. Time spent moving mail is time not spent on grout.</li><li><strong>Skip the oven\'s self-clean cycle that morning.</strong> Hautch warns it can trip sensors. Leave the oven as it is.</li><li><strong>Point the visit at kitchens and bathrooms.</strong> That is where the scrubbing hours go. Bedrooms that get a regular clean can stay standard if money is tight.</li></ul><h3>An Omaha deep cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Sweeping Beauty Cleaning Omaha, LLC</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering deep cleaning at your location in Omaha ZIP 68106. See its listing: <a href="/business/sweeping-beauty-cleaning-omaha-llc">Sweeping Beauty Cleaning Omaha, LLC on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 3 deep cleaning businesses in the Omaha metro, all covering ZIP 68106: <a href="/#/browse?zip=68106">search deep cleaning near 68106</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/deep-cleaning/omaha/">Deep cleaning in Omaha</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Keeping the home up after the reset? See the Omaha house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-omaha/">How much does house cleaning cost in Omaha?</a>, the Omaha handyman cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-a-handyman-cost-in-omaha/">How much does a handyman cost in Omaha?</a> and the Omaha mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-omaha/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Omaha?</a></p>{{img:2}}'
