      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Portland drivers actually pay</h3><p>Published Portland prices — three mobile lists, one Tigard shop list, and national figures labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Full detail, sedan / SUV or truck / large SUV (Bridge City, mobile)</td><td>$250 / $300 / $350</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail (Royal Detailing PDX, mobile)</td><td>$240</td></tr><tr><td>Exterior / interior detail (Royal)</td><td>$140 / $180</td></tr><tr><td>Interior only (Bridge City, mobile)</td><td>$150–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Full detail, starting — car / SUV or truck / large (Mad Dog, mobile)</td><td>$480 / $600 / $660</td></tr><tr><td>Interior detail, starting — car (Mad Dog, mobile)</td><td>$250</td></tr><tr><td>Complete detail, cars / SUVs and trucks / vans (Ace Cars, Tigard shop)</td><td>$269–$359 / $295–$385 / $325–$415</td></tr><tr><td>Interior detail, cars (Ace Cars, Tigard shop)</td><td>$169–$249</td></tr><tr><td>Engine detailing (Ace Cars, Tigard shop)</td><td>$85</td></tr><tr><td>Ceramic coating, starting — car (Mad Dog)</td><td>$800</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile detailing, national average (Thumbtack, national)</td><td>$144–$254</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $240 full detail and a $480 full detail aren’t two prices for the same work. Mad Dog’s $480 adds a one-step paint correction and paint protection to the inside-and-out clean. If your paint is fine and the cabin is the mess, that’s correction you never asked for. Read what’s in the package before you compare the number.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Portland?</h3><p><strong>Rain, sap, and moss set the Portland list.</strong> Armor Auto Detailing, a Portland-area mobile operator, puts it plainly: rain, road spray, tree sap, and mineral deposits leave paint dull even after a wash — and that’s before moss and pollen. Ace Cars in Tigard sets its final price by the same stuff — pet hair, water spots, tree sap, road tar, and paint oxidation are all named factors. Sap isn’t a quick wipe. It adds time, and time is the price.</p><p><strong>Size first, then condition.</strong> Bridge City charges $250, $300, or $350 by size alone, and says heavily soiled interiors and extreme pet hair may run higher, confirmed before work starts. Mad Dog prices pet hair removal as an add-on at $40 an hour and odor removal at $100. A clean sedan and a Tigard SUV that hauls a wet dog all winter aren’t the same job at any shop in town.</p><p><strong>Mobile in the rain is a real question here.</strong> Bridge City says interior details are generally possible rain or shine, though cover helps, and exterior work gets rescheduled if the forecast turns into a real downpour. Ask before you book a November appointment, not the morning of.</p><p><strong>Who brings water and power changes who can take the job.</strong> Bridge City needs a power outlet and, for exterior work, a hose at your place — interior-only can run without one. Royal says you need to provide nothing. In a Tigard apartment lot (97223), that difference decides the booking.</p><p><strong>Protection before the wet months pays back.</strong> Armor notes protection added after a clean helps grime release faster in the wet months — the car stays cleaner, and the next wash is cheaper work. A sealant added to a Tigard complete detail runs $80 at Ace Cars.</p><h3>How to pay less without a worse detail</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Buy the half that’s dirty.</strong> Interior-only runs $150–$250 at Bridge City and $180 at Royal. Exterior-only is $140 at Royal. A full detail is the wrong buy when one side is fine.</li><li><strong>Describe the car honestly before you book.</strong> Ace Cars gives an approximate price from a good description — age, dirt, pet hair, stains, sap — and sets the final price at the appointment. Photos do the same job.</li><li><strong>Skip the correction if the paint doesn’t need it.</strong> A flat full detail at $240–$350 covers the clean. Correction and ceramic work start at $480 and $800 at Mad Dog — worth it on a car you keep, hard to justify on one you’re selling soon.</li><li><strong>Ask about water and power up front.</strong> Tell the detailer what your driveway or lot has. Surprises on the day cost more than the question.</li></ul><h3>A Portland mobile detailing business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>Squeegee Detail</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering mobile auto detailing at your location in Tigard (97223) and Tigard (97224). See its listing: <a href="/business/squeegee-detail">Squeegee Detail on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 6 mobile auto detailing businesses in the Portland metro: <a href="/#/browse?zip=97223">search mobile detailing near 97223</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/mobile-auto-detailing/portland/">Mobile auto detailing in Portland</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>House needs work too? See the Portland house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-portland/">How much does house cleaning cost in Portland?</a></p><p>Comparing metros? See the Sioux Falls mobile car detailing cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-mobile-car-detailing-cost-in-sioux-falls/">How much does mobile car detailing cost in Sioux Falls?</a></p>{{img:2}}'
