      tldr: 'In Fargo, a standard house cleaning runs $110 to $235 on MaidProfit’s Fargo row, at $24 to $40 an hour per cleaner. Care.com puts an individual Fargo cleaner at about $22.27 an hour — solo cleaners, not companies. Bark puts a professional clean in Fargo at $150 on average, and size moves that number fast: $105 to $135 for a 1–2 bed home, $270 to $330 for a 5–6 bed home.',
      faq: [
        { q: 'How much does house cleaning cost in Fargo?', a: 'A standard clean runs $110 to $235 on MaidProfit’s Fargo row, at $24 to $40 an hour per cleaner. Bark puts a professional clean in Fargo at $150 on average, from $105–$135 for a 1–2 bed home to $270–$330 for a 5–6 bed home.' },
        { q: 'What does a standard house cleaning include in Fargo?', a: 'Care.com’s Fargo pages list the usual work: vacuuming, mopping, dusting, kitchen and bathroom cleaning, laundry, and basic organization. Deep cleaning, move-in or move-out work, and a cleaner using their own supplies can change the price.' },
        { q: 'How much does a deep clean cost in Fargo?', a: 'The North Dakota guide prices a deep clean for a 3-bedroom home at $190–$250, against $135–$170 for a standard visit. HomeGuide’s national figures put deep cleaning at $230–$600, labeled national.' },
        { q: 'Does booking regular cleaning in Fargo cost less per visit?', a: 'Usually, yes. HomeGuide’s national guide notes that many services offer discounts for weekly or monthly cleanings, and a home on a regular schedule rarely needs the pricier deep clean to get back to baseline.' },
        { q: 'How do I find house cleaning near me in Fargo?', a: 'Search Van Squads by ZIP. House cleaning coverage in the Fargo metro runs across ZIPs 58102, 58103, 58104, and 58105, with 14 businesses listed.' }
      ],
      body: '{{img:0}}<h3>What Fargo homeowners actually pay</h3><p>Prices from Fargo pages and North Dakota guides, plus national figures labeled national:</p><table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Typical price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Standard clean (MaidProfit, Fargo row)</td><td>$110–$235</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, per cleaner (MaidProfit, Fargo row)</td><td>$24–$40</td></tr><tr><td>Individual cleaner, average (Care.com, Fargo)</td><td>$22.27/hr</td></tr><tr><td>Individual cleaner, average starting rate (Care.com, Fargo cost page)</td><td>$21.98/hr</td></tr><tr><td>Professional clean, average (Bark, Fargo)</td><td>$150</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, 1–2 bed home (Bark, Fargo)</td><td>$105–$135</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, 3–4 bed home (Bark, Fargo)</td><td>$150–$195</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, 5–6 bed home (Bark, Fargo)</td><td>$270–$330</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, North Dakota (MaidProfit)</td><td>$100–$230 (avg $158)</td></tr><tr><td>Standard clean, 3-bed home, North Dakota (TheCleanestRoom, ND guide)</td><td>$135–$170 (state avg ~$155)</td></tr><tr><td>Deep clean, 3-bed home, North Dakota (TheCleanestRoom, ND guide)</td><td>$190–$250</td></tr><tr><td>Move-out clean, 3-bed home, North Dakota (TheCleanestRoom, ND guide)</td><td>$205–$280</td></tr><tr><td>Standard / deep clean, national (HomeGuide, national)</td><td>$90–$180 / $230–$600</td></tr><tr><td>Hourly, per cleaner, national (Thumbtack, national)</td><td>$25–$50</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This is where people overpay. A $110 standard visit and a $250 deep clean are not the same job at two prices. The standard visit keeps a lived-in home up — dusting, kitchen, bathrooms, floors. The deep clean goes after baseboards, vents, and the grime behind appliances. If your Fargo home gets cleaned every two weeks, budget from the standard row, not the deep row.</p>{{img:1}}<h3>What changes the price in Fargo?</h3><p><strong>Home size is the first lever.</strong> Bark’s Fargo page spreads a professional clean from $105–$135 for a 1–2 bed home to $270–$330 for a 5–6 bed home. MaidProfit’s Fargo row agrees on the spread, with standard visits at $110–$235. A quote that never asks your bed and bath count is a guess.</p><p><strong>Winter works its way inside.</strong> A North Dakota cost guide puts it plainly: the state’s hard winters make entryway, mudroom, and floor cleaning a recurring priority. Melted snow carries salt and grit across the floors of a home in 58103 or 58104 every week from November on. If your entryway needs real floor time at every visit, say so when you book — it’s cheaper to price it in than to have it added later.</p><p><strong>Fargo sits a little above the state line.</strong> Care.com’s Fargo cost page puts the average starting rate at $21.98 an hour, about 12% higher than the North Dakota average starting rate of $19.64. The same page puts Fargo about 1% above the national average starting rate of $21.66. You’re not paying big-city prices in Fargo, but you’re paying above the state average — and MaidProfit notes the western oil towns run higher still.</p><p><strong>First cleans and move-outs sit in their own tier.</strong> The North Dakota guide prices a 3-bedroom deep clean at $190–$250 and a move-out at $205–$280, against $135–$170 for a standard visit on the same size home. An empty apartment in 58102 gets checked room by room before a deposit comes back. Don’t budget that visit from the standard row.</p><h3>How to pay less and still get a clean house</h3><ul class="check-list"><li><strong>Book on a schedule.</strong> HomeGuide’s national guide notes that many cleaning services discount weekly or monthly bookings. A home cleaned every two weeks stays in standard-visit territory and skips the deep-clean reset.</li><li><strong>Clear the floors before the visit.</strong> Winter boots, entryway clutter, and laundry on the floor are minutes your cleaner spends tidying instead of cleaning. Those minutes are in your quote.</li><li><strong>Name the extras up front.</strong> Inside the fridge, inside the oven, and interior windows are add-ons at most companies. Priced in advance, they are a line item. Raised at the door, they reprice the whole visit.</li><li><strong>Compare the same job.</strong> Get two or three Fargo quotes for the same bed count, the same clean type, and the same extras. A $150 average from Bark is only useful against quotes built the same way.</li></ul><h3>A Fargo house cleaning business listed on Van Squads</h3><p><strong>TLC Cleaning</strong> is listed on Van Squads, offering house cleaning at your location in Fargo ZIPs 58102, 58103, 58104, and 58105. See its listing: <a href="/business/tlc-cleaning">TLC Cleaning on Van Squads</a>.</p><p>Van Squads lists 14 house cleaning businesses in the Fargo metro, covering ZIPs 58102, 58103, 58104, and 58105: <a href="/#/browse?zip=58103">search house cleaning near 58103</a>.</p><p>Want the whole list on one page? <a href="/house-cleaning/fargo/">House cleaning in Fargo</a> has every company Van Squads lists there, with phone numbers and service areas.</p><p>Comparing metros? See the Tulsa house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-tulsa/">How much does house cleaning cost in Tulsa?</a> and the Salt Lake City house cleaning cost guide: <a href="/blog/how-much-does-house-cleaning-cost-in-salt-lake-city/">How much does house cleaning cost in Salt Lake City?</a></p>{{img:2}}'
